okay good evening thank you for being  here this evening as  most of you already know we've received  a court order  to keep 30 of our voting sites open  until 8 pm  we've been in the process of contacting  all of those sites and the facilities  we have been successful in doing so we  don't anticipate any trouble in having  the extended hours  at any of our facilities  we've had hundreds of people working for  many many weeks  and leading into the election with  everything that's new this year  it's a tremendous amount of effort that  we have with our staff  i have to commend them it's been a very  challenging year not just for the  election support but  with the pandemic several challenges  that uh were unexpected but they've done  an excellent job in providing access  for voters in clark county  earlier we did have technical issues  that we experienced at sites  the majority of those issues dealt with  connectivity and the setup of our poll  books where we signed people in to vote  in some cases we had a few issues very  small but there were some issues with  machines  are they throughout the day  it's in the morning connectivity is an  issue that we experience throughout the  day  much like people who go home after five  when a majority of the public starts to  sign in  on their smart devices there's a slow in  the connectivity of all of their devices  we experience that all day long so it's  a challenge that we deal with  we had good admin rover support today  they were able to respond and we did get  all polling places back up and running  nothing out of the ordinary and again we  have a strong team of admin rovers who  travel throughout the valley  we quickly respond we had a tremendous  amount of support  from local law enforcement along with  the mac center that was open today and  the secretary of state  with the support that we had we were  able to handle all issues  voters leading into election day we had  378 000  early voters and we had reported a  little over 400 000 mail ballots  received we're still in the process of  crossing  assessing some of those but the  challenges that we dealt with were  tremendous  the pandemic being one of the most major  has  and it resulted in what we had to do in  the primary election we made  considerable changes to make sure that  we had an increase in access we went  from one election day polling  three excuse me election day polling  sites in the primary and one early  voting site  to 35 sites that were open for 14 days  and 125 vote centers that were available  today for voting so  putting all that together getting the  poll workers uh dealing with the  poll worker group that is majority of  seniors who were more susceptible to the  pandemic  was a challenge that we dealt with  consistently but we were successful  in getting the workers that we needed so  no absolutely not we have mail coming in  there are mail ballot drop-off locations  at all 125 of our sites plus the  election department  plus the u.s mail we're required to wait  for those to come in as well so what you  see tonight will be an unofficial report  and it won't be final until november  16th  today i don't know if it was a record  turnout for for the in person  because it's difficult to gauge because  there was drop off and we don't know how  many there are there but early voting  the mail that we received so far and our  in-person early voting was definitely a  large increase  in what we've seen in the past  well we're not done yet so i can't  really give you that report however  during the course of the day we had  lines that were  average i would say that the turnout  today the last time we checked was at  about 68 000  which is a considerable amount lower  than what we normally see  election day we were prepared to handle  well over two hundred thousand voters on  election day but we're  not going to get anywhere near that  well without a doubt the early voting we  had a full early voting program in fact  we had three more sites this year  than we did in 2018 as was required  through ab4  and then the vote centers that we put in  place it's 122 more sites so  yes  well the report is going to be later  obviously and it'll  probably affect the whole state because  we can't report in any county in the  state of nevada until the secretary of  state  has confirmed with us that all voters  are done in the entire state of nevada  so as a result of us staying open until  8 pm  it's going to slow down the election  results coming out  machines do not come back to the polling  to the election center  they start being picked up tomorrow as  far as the ballots  they are secured by the two team leaders  that are assigned at each vote center  and they will be bringing those back  tonight with us but the police  escort is for our transport from trade  drive to graystone where we process  ballots  [Music]  sure it's important that if the general  public is not confident in the integrity  of the process  that they're not confident that their  vote counts then  the election isn't effective and so  we've always worked here it's been our  number one priority  to uphold the integrity and everything  that we do although we've seen a  tremendous increase in the number of  male ballots  we have been doing male ballots for many  years and so we had to  redefine our processes to handle the  number of mail ballots however  we were very comfortable with the  process that we had in place  every presidential election for an  election official is the biggest  election they've done  especially in a jurisdiction like clark  county where we have continued growth  this is my eighth presidential election  so i would have to say that this has  probably been the most difficult  election i've ever had to support  [Music]  absolutely the pressure has come from  many different groups both parties uh  third-party community  uh partners that we have in the  community everybody was very engaged in  this election and wanted to make sure  that their vote was going to count and  that our processes would hold up  with the changes that we've had as a  result of the pandemic  and going to all mail for all active  registered voters  so we have also been doing a tremendous  amount of outreach with our general  public  through psas and also in doing several  zoom meetings uh with different groups  to make sure that they were aware of the  changes  and aware of all of the access that we  were working hard to provide  it was a challenge and we had to make  sure that  we were providing a process that made  them feel comfortable  that they would have access to the  ballot and i believe we were successful  that comes with a job that's not unique  to this election  i'm an umpire in the worst baseball game  in the world and i have to keep it fair  and so that's  if you're not prepared for that you  shouldn't be an election official  well we can't close the pose until late  and if you're in line at eight o'clock  at any of those 30 sites  we're gonna put a staffer at the end of  the line so there's no guarantee  that those sites will close at eight we  will continue to process voters  if they're in line at eight o'clock so  it's difficult for me to predict  exactly when but it's going to be later  than we anticipate  so there were 125 boat centers  throughout clark county each one of  those locations  has to return our flash drive so that we  can read them into the system  we will verify that all cartridges have  been received  before we close out on our final  unofficial report for this evening  all of those team leaders will come  through the doors directly behind me  and they'll be bringing in paperwork uh  bail ballot drop-off boxes  to be secured and the flash drives that  we need to read into the system so all  of that needs to be complete before we  can put out our final unofficial

